{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan review BLOCKED, and the reviewer was right on all three findings. I verified them against the tree before editing.\n\nThe plan claimed validate and Finding must both stay importable from rebar._cli._registry because test_capabilities, test_cli_registry and test_cli_registry_dispatch all import them from there. False in specifics: test_capabilities and test_cli_registry import Route, validate; test_cli_registry_dispatch imports the module handle (from rebar._cli import _execute, _registry, main). None of the three imports Finding, and NOTHING in the tree imports Finding from rebar._cli._registry — the only Finding import anywhere is from the unrelated check_ssm_secret_state module.\n\nReplaced the assumption with a census. 22 files reference rebar._cli._registry; across named imports and module-handle attribute access they consume exactly eight names: ROUTES, Route, validate, route_for, derive_policy_sets, ADAPTER_KINDS, INIT_POLICIES, KNOWN_CAPABILITIES. Of the cluster being moved only validate is externally consumed, so only validate needs the back-compat re-export; Finding is the cluster own return type and moves with it. AC2 now asserts those eight names resolve on the module after the split, which is a stronger and checkable postcondition than the three-test claim it replaces.\n\nWorth noting for anyone repeating the census: my first scoped grep undercounted, because it matched \"from rebar._cli import _registry\" exactly and missed the dispatch test importing three names on one line. The 22-file figure comes from a pattern covering all three import shapes.\n\nRe-review started."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788400284788436001,"uuid":"baa649dc-5e75-466a-8c47-db67c47dc948"}